IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-76, TARGETED: the Regulation of Investment Advice, Investment Marketing and Portfolio Management Law, 5755-1995 ("the Law"). Draft, target compiler main. No domain expert has read this against the source.
-- THIS ROW DOES NOT ENCODE THE LAW. It records one item (I1), an amending instruction and the clause it names, as typed values, and tests them.
-- SEAT: the individual who reads the printed instruments to see which words the pages print. A row of references asks that individual no question: there is no input to ask for, and no @export.
-- NOUNS: an instrument of Sefer HaChukim, a place in the Law, the heading of an instruction set on the Law, the instruction of 2024 that puts words after an anchor word, the instruction of 2011 that writes a paragraph, the instruction of 2013 that names that paragraph, a printed clause, a commencement as the page prints it, an instrument read and not deposited, the item, and the questions asked of them.
-- No reference is stated here; they are in iv76-cross-references.l4.
--
-- The item is recorded with two limbs, as in the other targeted rows:
--   limb (a): the target is repealed, missing or says something else, read from an official instrument;
--   limb (b): the citing words still read so in the latest official instrument read.
-- Subsection letters are written with Latin names for the Hebrew letters the Law uses: (א) is Alef and (ב) is Bet.
-- THE NAMES BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's. A date typed as an issue date is the date the footer of the issue prints; it is NOT a commencement date.
-- A commencement is typed separately, and only where a page prints one.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `A way a fact was read` IS ONE OF
    `official page image`
    `official page image, with the instruments listed in NOTES.md`
    `CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `not deposited, not shown by any deposit of this row`
    `not checked`

DECLARE `A subsection letter` IS ONE OF
    Alef
    Bet

-- An issue of Sefer HaChukim. The issue date is the one the footer prints.
-- The title is typed only where a deposited page prints it (the cover of the issue); otherwise it is NOTHING.
DECLARE `An instrument` HAS
    `its issue of Sefer HaChukim` IS A NUMBER
    `its issue date` IS A DATE
    `its title as a deposited page prints it` IS A MAYBE STRING

-- A place in the Law: a section, optionally a subsection, optionally a paragraph of it.
-- A paragraph label is typed as the page prints it, with its parentheses, numeral first and letter after it where there is one.
DECLARE `A place in the Law` HAS
    `its section` IS A NUMBER
    `its subsection` IS A MAYBE `A subsection letter`
    `its paragraph label` IS A MAYBE STRING

-- The heading under which an instrument prints its instructions on the Law: the section number, the heading words, the margin note and the cover's line for the Law.
-- A margin note or a cover line is typed only where a deposited page shows it; otherwise it is NOTHING.
DECLARE `An instruction set on the Law` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page of its heading` IS A NUMBER
    `the section of the instrument` IS A NUMBER
    `the heading words as printed` IS A STRING
    `the margin note as printed` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `the cover's line for the Law as printed` IS A MAYBE STRING

-- A clause as an instrument printed it: the words between the closing marks, as one string and as the list of its words split on spaces.
-- `the count the row types` is the number of times the page shows the anchor word in the clause, counted on the band and on the list.
DECLARE `A printed clause` HAS
    `the instrument that printed it` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page it is on` IS A NUMBER
    `the item that prints it` IS A STRING
    `the place it is printed for` IS A `A place in the Law`
    `its words as one string` IS A STRING
    `its words split on spaces` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the count the row types` IS A NUMBER

-- An instruction that writes a paragraph: it says after which paragraph the clause comes, and the clause is the one it prints.
DECLARE `An instruction that writes a paragraph` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page it is on` IS A NUMBER
    `the section of the instrument` IS A NUMBER
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the place it names` IS A `A place in the Law`
    `the paragraph it prints the clause after` IS A STRING
    `the clause it prints` IS A `A printed clause`

-- An instruction that puts words after an anchor word.
-- It is typed as the components the page prints, and nothing is said about where the words go.
DECLARE `An instruction that puts words after an anchor word` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page it is on` IS A NUMBER
    `the section of the instrument` IS A NUMBER
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the place it names` IS A `A place in the Law`
    `the word it prints before the anchor word` IS A STRING
    `the anchor word` IS A STRING
    `the word it prints before the words put in` IS A STRING
    `the words put in` IS A STRING

-- An instruction that names a paragraph as the place after which something comes. No word of the paragraph it names is typed, and the words it puts are not deposited.
DECLARE `An instruction that names a paragraph to come after` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page it is on` IS A NUMBER
    `the section of the instrument` IS A NUMBER
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the place it names` IS A `A place in the Law`
    `the paragraph it names` IS A STRING
    `the words it puts` IS A MAYBE STRING

-- A commencement as read. The number of months is typed only where the page prints it as words for a period; the date only where the page prints a calendar date.
DECLARE `A commencement as printed` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page it is on` IS A NUMBER
    `the section of the instrument` IS A NUMBER
    `the subsection` IS A STRING
    `its words as printed` IS A STRING
    `the number of months after publication the page prints` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the date the page prints` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- An instrument read and not deposited: what its page printed about section 39, in English, as the record of the reading.
-- Nothing in this row shows it; the status is `not deposited, not shown by any deposit of this row`.
DECLARE `An instrument read and not deposited` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed pages read` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    `what the pages printed about section 39` IS A STRING
    `how it was read` IS A `A way a fact was read`

-- The item of the row, with its two limbs.
DECLARE `An item` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the target is in` IS A STRING
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `A way a fact was read`
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `A way a fact was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

-- ===== QUESTIONS ASKED OF THE VALUES =====

-- How many tokens of the list are the word, whole.
GIVEN w IS A STRING, ts IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of times the word occurs among the words` MEANS count (filter (GIVEN t YIELD t EQUALS w) ts)

-- The positions, counting from the number n, at which the word is a token of the list.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, w IS A STRING, ts IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the positions of the word from` MEANS
    CONSIDER ts
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF x EQUALS w
        THEN n FOLLOWED BY `the positions of the word from` (n PLUS 1) w rest
        ELSE `the positions of the word from` (n PLUS 1) w rest

-- The words joined with one space between each, to compare the list with the one string.
GIVEN ts IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the words joined with single spaces` MEANS
    CONSIDER ts
    WHEN EMPTY THEN ""
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN foldl (GIVEN acc, t YIELD CONCAT acc, " ", t) x rest

GIVEN c IS A `A printed clause`, w IS A STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of times the word occurs in the clause` MEANS `the number of times the word occurs among the words` w (c's `its words split on spaces`)

GIVEN i IS AN `An instruction that puts words after an anchor word`, c IS A `A printed clause`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of times the anchor word occurs in the clause` MEANS `the number of times the word occurs in the clause` c (i's `the anchor word`)

-- I1, the question the red assertion asks: does the anchor word occur exactly once in the clause as printed?
GIVEN i IS AN `An instruction that puts words after an anchor word`, c IS A `A printed clause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the anchor word occurs exactly once in the clause` MEANS `the number of times the anchor word occurs in the clause` i c EQUALS 1

GIVEN i IS AN `An instruction that puts words after an anchor word`, c IS A `A printed clause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the anchor word occurs in the clause at least once` MEANS `the number of times the anchor word occurs in the clause` i c > 0

GIVEN i IS AN `An instruction that puts words after an anchor word`, c IS A `A printed clause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the words put in are contained in the clause` MEANS CONTAINS (c's `its words as one string`) (i's `the words put in`)

-- Two places are the same place: the same section, subsection and paragraph label.
GIVEN a IS A `A place in the Law`, b IS A `A place in the Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two places are the same place` MEANS
    (a's `its section` EQUALS b's `its section`)
    AND (a's `its subsection` EQUALS b's `its subsection`)
    AND (a's `its paragraph label` EQUALS b's `its paragraph label`)

-- The label of the clause is the first word of its list.
GIVEN c IS A `A printed clause`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the label the clause begins with` MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `its words split on spaces`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST x

GIVEN a IS AN `An instrument`, b IS AN `An instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the first instrument was issued after the second` MEANS a's `its issue date` > b's `its issue date`

GIVEN a IS AN `An instrument`, b IS AN `An instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two instruments are two different issues` MEANS NOT (a's `its issue of Sefer HaChukim` EQUALS b's `its issue of Sefer HaChukim`)
